               \           |       /
                \          |      /
                 \         |     /
                  \        |    /
                   \       |   /
                    \      |  /
                     \     | /
                      \    |/
                       \   |
                        \  |
                         \ |
                          \|
        Server B (105) ----+---- Server C (110)
                          /|
                         / |
                        /  |
                       /   |
                      /    |
                     /     |
                    /      |
                   /       |
                  /        |
                 /         |
                /          |
               /           |
              /            |
             /             |
            /              |
           /               |
          /                |
         /                 |
        180                |



Ab dekho har server ka preceding arc (kitna ring portion usse handle karna hai):

Server	  Preceding Arc   	Kitna Portion 	 Load
A (100)	  300 → 360 → 100	160 units	     Zyada
B (105)	  100 → 105	        5 units	         Bahut Kam
C (110)	  105 → 110	        5 units	         Bahut Kam
D (300)	  110 → 300	        190 units	     Zyada


Result:

- Server A aur Server D → zyada load (bada arc)
- Server B aur Server C → almost idle (chhota arc)

Yaani B aur C servers baithe rehte hain khaali, jabki A aur D overloaded hote hain.

Isi ko Uneven Distribution ya Hot Spot kehte hain.



### QUESTION : UNEVEN SERVER DISTRIBUTION ON THE RING KA SOLUTION ? - VIRTUAL NODES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Simple Consistent Hashing me ek physical server ko ring par sirf ek position
par place kiya jaata hai. Isi wajah se hot spot problem aati hai i.e kuch
servers ke paas bada arc hota hai (more traffic), kuch ke paas chhota (Less traffic).

## QUESTION : VIRTUAL NODE KYA HAI ?
--------------------------------------

Virtual Node ka matlab hai — ek physical server ko hash ring par sirf
ek position par nahi, balki multiple positions par place karna. 
aise karne se Ek physical server ka total load =  uske saare virtual nodes ke arcs ka sum


## EXAMPLE — SAME 4 SERVERS, LEKIN AB VIRTUAL NODES KE SAATH
---------------------------------------------------------------

Same 4 servers:

    Server A
    Server B
    Server C
    Server D

Ab har server ko 3-3 virtual nodes dete hain.

Conceptually:

    Server A → V-A-1, V-A-2, V-A-3
    Server B → V-B-1, V-B-2, V-B-3
    Server C → V-C-1, V-C-2, V-C-3
    Server D → V-D-1, V-D-2, V-D-3

Ab in sab virtual nodes ka identifier hash karke ring par place karte hain.

Maan lo hash function ka range 0 to 360 hai.



Ring par positions aisi mili:

    V-A-1 → 30
    V-B-1 → 80
    V-C-1 → 140
    V-D-1 → 200

    V-A-2 → 240
    V-B-2 → 270
    V-C-2 → 300
    V-D-2 → 330

    V-A-3 → 10
    V-B-3 → 50
    V-C-3 → 170
    V-D-3 → 360


Ring par (sorted order me):

    10  → V-A-3
    30  → V-A-1
    50  → V-B-3
    80  → V-B-1
    140 → V-C-1
    170 → V-C-3
    200 → V-D-1
    240 → V-A-2
    270 → V-B-2
    300 → V-C-2
    330 → V-D-2
    360 → V-D-3


Ab har virtual node apne preceding arc ka traffic handle karega:

    Virtual Node    Preceding Arc       Arc Size
    ---------------------------------------------------
    V-A-3  (10)     360 → 10            10 units
    V-A-1  (30)     10  → 30            20 units
    V-B-3  (50)     30  → 50            20 units
    V-B-1  (80)     50  → 80            30 units
    V-C-1  (140)    80  → 140           60 units
    V-C-3  (170)    140 → 170           30 units
    V-D-1  (200)    170 → 200           30 units
    V-A-2  (240)    200 → 240           40 units
    V-B-2  (270)    240 → 270           30 units
    V-C-2  (300)    270 → 300           30 units
    V-D-2  (330)    300 → 330           30 units
    V-D-3  (360)    330 → 360           30 units


Ab physical server ke total load ko add karo:

    Server A  → V-A-3 (10) + V-A-1 (20) + V-A-2 (40)
              → Total = 70 units

    Server B  → V-B-3 (20) + V-B-1 (30) + V-B-2 (30)
              → Total = 80 units

    Server C  → V-C-1 (60) + V-C-3 (30) + V-C-2 (30)
              → Total = 120 units

    Server D  → V-D-1 (30) + V-D-2 (30) + V-D-3 (30)
              → Total = 90 units


Compare karo:

    Without Virtual Nodes:

        Server A → 160 units  (overloaded)
        Server B →   5 units  (almost idle)
        Server C →   5 units  (almost idle)
        Server D → 190 units  (overloaded)


    With Virtual Nodes:

        Server A →  70 units
        Server B →  80 units
        Server C → 120 units
        Server D →  90 units


Load ab bahut zyada even ho gaya. Har server ke paas reasonably equal
traffic aa raha hai. Yehi Virtual Nodes ka main fayda hai.




