# QUESTION : API GATEWAY KYA HOTA HAI AUR YE KYA PROBLEM SOLVE KARTA HAI ?
============================================================================

Socho API Gateway nahi hai. Architecture kuch aisi hogi:

                           Client / User
                                |
      -------------------------------------------------------
      |                          |                          |
      v                          v                          v
 user-service.company.com   order-service.company.com   payment-service.company.com
        (URL)                     (URL)                      (URL)
      |                          |                          |
      | DNS Resolution           | DNS Resolution           | DNS Resolution
      v                          v                          v
 User Service LB (IP)      Order Service LB (IP)      Payment Service LB (IP)
      |                          |                          |
      v                          v                          v
 User Instances            Order Instances           Payment Instances


## PROBLEMS :
----------------

1. Client ko har service ke Load Balancer ka endpoint
   (typically ek URL / CNAME) apne paas maintain karna padega.
   Har request ke time client us URL ka DNS Resolution karke
   corresponding Load Balancer ka IP obtain karega.

2. Jaise-jaise microservices ki sankhya badhti jaati hai,
   client ko aur bhi zyada service LB endpoints maintain karne
   padte hain. Ye architecture maintain karna difficult ho jata hai.

3. Agar future me kisi service LB ka endpoint change ho jaye,
   to client ko bhi update karna padega.

4. Authentication, Authorization, Rate Limiting, Logging jaise
   common functionalities bhi har service me alag-alag
   implement karni pad sakti hain. Isse duplication aur
   maintenance overhead badh jaata hai.


## SOLUTION : API GATEWAY
----------------------------

In problems ko solve karne ke liye API Gateway introduce kiya jata hai.

API Gateway koi physical hardware device nahi hota — ye ek software
application hota hai jo client requests ke liye Single Entry Point
provide karta hai, aur ek normal application ki tarah ek ya multiple
servers par run karta hai.

Ab client ko sirf API Gateway ka endpoint / URL pata hona chahiye —
baaki kis service ke LB tak request bhejni hai, ye responsibility
API Gateway ki hoti hai.

Isse:

    - Client ko ek hi endpoint yaad rakhna padta hai.
    - Services ke LB add/remove/change hone par client ko update
      nahi karna padta.
    - Common functionalities (Auth, Rate Limiting, Logging)
      ek hi jagah centralized ho jaati hain.

Isliye API Gateway ko client aur microservices ke beech ek
centralized entry point ki tarah use kiya jata hai.

Examples:

    - Spring Cloud Gateway
    - Kong
    - NGINX
    - Traefik
    - Envoy
    - AWS API Gateway



--------------------------------------------
## QUESTION : API GATEWAY KYA KARTA HAI ?
--------------------------------------------

### 1. REQUEST ROUTING
------------------------

API Gateway incoming request ka URL check karta hai aur request ko
appropriate microservice ke Load Balancer tak forward karta hai.

Example:

    /users/**      → User Service Load Balancer
    /orders/**     → Order Service Load Balancer
    /payments/**   → Payment Service Load Balancer



### 2. AUTHENTICATION AND AUTHORIZATION
------------------------------------------

JWT issue ek dedicated Auth Service karta hai (API Gateway nahi).
Uske baad subsequent requests ko authenticate aur authorize karne
ka kaam API Gateway kar sakta hai.

Gateway par JWT validate hota hai, aur validation ke baad backend
ko headers me user info bhejta hai — jaise X-User-Id, X-User-Roles.
Backend services JWT nahi padhti, headers trust karti hain.

Authentication ke baad Gateway verify karta hai ki user requested
resource access karne ke liye authorized hai ya nahi.

Iska fayda: 100 microservices me duplicate JWT authentication /
authorization code nahi likhna padta.


### 3. RATE LIMITING
---------------------
(Already discussed in L7 LB section)


### 4. SSL/TLS TERMINATION
----------------------------
(Already discussed in L7 LB section)


### 5. REQUEST TRANSFORMATION
------------------------------
(Already discussed in L7 LB section)


### 6. RESPONSE TRANSFORMATION
------------------------------
(Already discussed in L7 LB section)


### 7. COMPRESSION
--------------------
(Already discussed in L7 LB section)


### 8. API VERSIONING
----------------------

API Gateway multiple API versions support kar sakta hai.

Example:

    /api/v1/users    →  User Service V1 Load Balancer
    /api/v2/users    →  User Service V2 Load Balancer

Gateway URL me version dekh kar request ko corresponding version
ke backend tak route kar deta hai.


#### NOTE:
-----------

V1 aur V2 generally User Service ke different deployed versions
hote hain — har version ke multiple instances aur apna Load
Balancer ho sakta hai.

Lekin ye bhi possible hai ki V1/V2 alag deployments ke bajaye
same User Service ke andar different endpoints ke through
implement kiye gaye hon. Ye architecture par depend karta hai.



#### QUESTION : API VERSIONING KI ZARURAT KYA HAI ?
------------------------------------------------------

##### PROBLEM :
----------------

Tumhari API already live hai. Hazaaron mobile apps use kar rahe hain.
Ab tum kuch change karna chahte ho — lekin purane clients ko todna nahi chahte.

##### SOLUTION :
-----------------

Live API me breaking changes introduce karne ke liye, bina
purane clients ko tode. Purana version chalne dete hain
jab tak clients naye version par migrate na ho jaayein.


##### EXAMPLE :
----------------

    V1 API (already live — 10,000 clients use kar rahe hain):

        GET /api/v1/users/101
        Response: { "id": 101, "name": "Anurag" }


    Ab requirement: "name" ko hatao aur uske jagah do naye fields
    "firstName" and "lastName" karo (breaking change).


    Agar seedha V1 API me change kar do:
        → purane clients "name" dhundhenge, crash ho jaayenge


    Sahi approach — Naya version banao:

        V1 (purane clients ke liye unchanged):
            GET /api/v1/users/101
            { "id": 101, "name": "Anurag" }

        V2 (naye clients ke liye):
            GET /api/v2/users/101
            { "id": 101, "firstName": "Anurag", "lastName": "Pandey" }



##### DONO VERSIONS KE SERVICES ALAG-ALAG DEPLOY KARO
--------------------------------------------------------

V1 aur V2 ke liye corresponding services alag deploy karo —
har version ke apne instances aur apna Load Balancer.

                    API Gateway
                          |
            ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
            v                           v
    /api/v1/**                    /api/v2/**
            |                           |
            v                           v
    User Service V1 LB            User Service V2 LB
            |                           |
            v                           v
    V1 Instances                  V2 Instances
    (name field)                  (firstName, lastName)


API Gateway URL me version dekh kar request ko corresponding
version ke Load Balancer tak route kar deta hai.


##### DEPRECATION
--------------------

Kuch time baad — jab sab clients V2 pe migrate ho jaayein,
V1 ko deprecate kar do:

    1. V1 ko deprecated mark karo (docs me)
    2. Clients ko migrate hone ka warning bhejo
    3. Migration deadline set karo
    4. Deadline ke baad V1 services band karo




### 9. LOGGING
-----------------

API Gateway har incoming request aur outgoing response ka log
maintain kar sakta hai.

Example Logged Data:

    Client IP, HTTP Method, URL,
    Response Status, Response Time, Timestamp



### 10. MONITORING
-------------------

Gateway operational metrics collect karke monitoring systems
(Prometheus, Grafana, CloudWatch) ko bhej sakta hai.

Examples: Average Latency, P95/P99 Latency, RPS, Error Rate,
CPU/Memory usage.



### 11. CIRCUIT BREAKING 
---------------------------

Suppose koi downstream service (e.g. Payment Service) repeatedly
fail ho rahi hai.

Agar Gateway har request us service ko forward karta rahe, to:

    - Unnecessary network calls hongi
    - Failing service par aur load padega
    - Cascading failures ka risk badhega

Is situation me Circuit Breaker temporarily "Open" ho jata hai.

Circuit Open hone par Gateway us service ko request forward nahi
karta — immediately client ko fallback/error response return kar
deta hai:

    503 Service Unavailable

                OR

    "Payment Service is temporarily unavailable. Please try again later."

Isse unnecessary requests aur cascading failures avoid ho jaate hain.



### 12. LOAD BALANCING 
-------------------------

Kuch API Gateways (depending on implementation) khud bhi load balancing kar sakte hain. 
Ye URL routing ke baad, us service ke available instances me traffic
distribute kar dete hain:

        /users/**  →  User Service instances me load balance
        /orders/** →  Order Service instances me load balance


#### NOTE:
------------

Production me commonly API Gateway ke
baad dedicated Service Load Balancers ya Service Discovery
mechanisms (Eureka, Consul, Kubernetes Services) instances ko
discover aur load balance karte hain.





