# QUESTION : CDN KYA HOTA HAI AUR YE KYA PROBLEM SOLVE KARTA HAI ?
=====================================================================

CDN = Content Delivery Network.

CDNs geographically distributed servers hote hain jo different
locations (Mumbai, Singapore, London, Virginia) me deployed hote
hain. In locations ko CDN Edge Locations kehte hain.

CDN ka primary purpose: frequently requested content ko user ke
nearby CDN Edge se serve karna, taaki Origin tak baar-baar
request na jaaye.


## MAIN BENEFITS
-----------------

Static content cache karna — Images, Videos, CSS, JS, Fonts.

Isse Origin load reduce hota hai (cached content CDN Edge se
serve hota hai), aur CDN Edge user ke nearby hota hai, jiski
wajah se network latency reduce hoti hai aur response faster
milta hai.


## QUESTION : CDN KO KAISE PATA CACHE KARNA HAI YA NAHI ? AUR CACHE KAB EXPIRE HOTA HAI ?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CDN khud decide nahi karta. Origin Server se jo response aata hai,
uske headers me hi specified hota hai ki usse cache karna hai ya
nahi, aur kitni der tak:

    Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
        → 24 hours tak cache karo

    Cache-Control: no-store
        → Cache mat karo, har request Origin tak jaayegi


TTL (Time To Live) max-age ke according set hota hai. TTL expire
hone ke baad:

    → CDN cache entry remove ho jaati hai
    → Next request → Cache Miss → Origin se fresh content fetch


### NOTE:
----------
Agar immediately content update karna ho (TTL wait karne ke bina),
to CDN manually bhi purge kar sakta hai (admin panel / API se).



## QUESTION : IMAGE UPDATE HONE KE BAAD BHI CDN PURANI IMAGE KYUN DIKHA RAHA HAI ?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Kyunki CDN ke paas wahi image cached hai — Origin par update hone
ka CDN ko automatically pata nahi chalta. Jab tak TTL expire na ho
ya manually purge na karo, purani image serve hoti rahegi.


SOLUTION:

1. Short TTL rakho (frequently updated content ke liye)
2. Manually purge karo (critical content ke liye)
3. Versioned URLs use karo (sabse common)

       /images/product-101.jpg → /images/product-101-v2.jpg

   Jab image update ho, uska naam/URL hi change kar do.
   Isse naya URL CDN cache me milega hi nahi → Cache Miss →
   Origin se fresh image fetch hogi.

   Fayda: Purani image ke TTL expiry ka wait nahi karna padta,
   aur manually purge karne ki bhi zaroorat nahi padti.



## QUESTION : KYA CDN DYNAMIC APIs KO CACHE KAR SAKTA HAI ?
-------------------------------------------------------------

CDNs mostly static content cache karte hain. Lekin cacheable dynamic
GET responses bhi cache ho sakte hain — agar data frequently change
nahi hota aur Origin appropriate caching headers ke through allow kare.

Example:

    GET /products → Cache-Control: public, max-age=60
    → 60 seconds tak CDN se serve hoga, backend tak request nahi jaayegi.

POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE generally cache nahi hote — ye state
change karte hain.




## DNS AUR CDN KA BEHAVIOUR
-----------------------------

Case 4.1 : Anycast IP Based CDN

    Multiple CDN Edge Locations same IP address announce kar sakti hain,
    aur ye same IP DNS me configured ho sakta hai. DNS resolution ke baad
    CDN ka IP return hota hai. Uske baad BGP routing automatically request
    ko nearest/optimal CDN Edge tak route karti hai.

    Example:

        User in India  →  Nearby CDN Edge (e.g. Mumbai / Singapore)
        User in US     →  Nearby CDN Edge (e.g. Virginia)

    User ko generally pata bhi nahi hota ki request kis CDN Edge ne serve
    ki. Network routing automatically appropriate CDN Edge select karti hai.


Case 4.2 : Geo DNS Based CDN

    Different CDN Edge Locations ke different IP addresses ho sakte hain.
    DNS resolver user ki approximate geographical location ke basis par
    nearby CDN IP return kar sakta hai.

    Example:

        User India me hai   →  DNS returns India / Singapore CDN IP
        User Europe me hai  →  DNS returns Europe CDN IP



## QUESTION : CDN KAISE HELP KARTA HAI ?
------------------------------------------

Without CDN:
    Har request Origin tak travel karti hai.

With CDN:
    First Request  → CDN Edge → Cache Miss → Origin → Cache & Return
    Subsequent     → CDN Edge → Cache Hit  → Direct return (Origin tak request nahi jaati)



## QUESTION : CDN vs REDIS ?
------------------------------

CDN   → User ke nearby content cache karta hai (network latency
        kam karne ke liye). TTL Cache-Control header ke max-age
        attribute se set hota hai.

Redis → Mostly database aur application ke beech hota hai, aur
        database results (mostly GET responses) ko RAM me store
        karta hai — taaki DB par kam load jaaye. TTL application
        commands ke through define karta hai (SETEX / EXPIRE).




