## QUESTION : SIGNED URLS KYA HOTE HAIN ?
===========================================

Signed URL ek temporary URL hota hai jise use karke cloud storage
(S3, GCS) me stored private files ko bina login access kiya ja
sakta hai.

Is URL me 3 cheezein hoti hain:

    - File ka path (bucket + object key)
    - Expiry time (kab tak valid)
    - Cryptographic signature (proof ki URL legitimate hai)


### USE CASE:
---------------

Cloud storage me files private hoti hain by default. Lekin
kabhi-kabhi user ko specific file temporarily deni hoti hai:

    - Bank statement PDF download
    - KYC document upload / view
    - Invoice / receipt PDF
    - Private profile picture


### QUESTION : SIGNED URL GENERATE KARNE KE APPROACHES ?
----------------------------------------------------------

#### APPROACH 1 : SYMMETRIC (S3 Pre-Signed URLs)
-------------------------------------------------

Application ke paas Secret Access Key hoti hai (AWS credentials).
Wahi key Amazon S3 ke paas bhi stored hai (kyunki AWS ne hi generate
ki thi jab account banaya).


FLOW:

1. User private file access karna chahta hai (jaise bank statement download).
2. Backend Secret Key se sign karke signed URL generate karta hai.
3. Backend ye signed URL user ko return karta hai.
4. User signed URL par request bhejta hai → S3.
5. S3 apni stored Secret Key se signature verify karta hai.

        Valid   → File serve
        Invalid → 403 Forbidden


EXAMPLE:

        https://bank-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/statement-101.pdf
        ?X-Amz-Expires=900
        &X-Amz-Signature=ABC123XYZ...

        User ye URL 15 min ke andar open karke file download kar
        sakta hai. 15 min ke baad URL invalid → 403 Forbidden.



#### APPROACH 2 : ASYMMETRIC (CloudFront Signed URLs)
-------------------------------------------------------

Application ke paas Private Key hoti hai.
CloudFront ke paas corresponding Public Key hoti hai.


FLOW:

1. User private file access karna chahta hai.
2. Backend Private Key se sign karke signed URL generate karta hai.
3. Backend ye signed URL user ko return karta hai.
4. User signed URL par request bhejta hai → CloudFront.
5. CloudFront Public Key se signature verify karta hai.

        Valid   → File serve
        Invalid → 403 Forbidden
